%% NOTE: Keep this diagram updated with any protocol or flow changes!
%% Last updated: 2026-03-26
sequenceDiagram
    title: Event Update Flow (Maintenance Window Backlog Drain) (DEPRECATED)
    autonumber
    box Device Agent
        participant Agent as Agent v2
    end
    box Fleet
        participant Fleet as Fleet Manager
    end
    box eLabFTW
        participant Event as /event/{id}
    end
    Note over Agent,Event: Derived diagram. Source of truth: lifecycle-v2-normalized.mmd

    Note over Agent,Fleet: DEPRECATED diagram. Use event-write-flow.mmd as canonical flow.
    Note over Agent,Fleet: Report replay is gated by maintenance_window(from/to) + slot+jitter.
    Agent->>Agent: Evaluate maintenance window + device slot
    alt outside maintenance window/slot
        Agent->>Agent: Keep runs in pending spool\nskip PublishReport
    else inside maintenance window+slot
        Agent->>Agent: Select next local pending run
        Agent->>Fleet: PublishReport(next event batch)
        Fleet->>Event: PATCH metadata(state=REPORT_RECEIVED)
        Note over Fleet: run mapping + dedupe handled internally
        Fleet->>Event: GET /event/{id}
        Event-->>Fleet: current metadata
        Fleet->>Event: PATCH metadata\n(events[], last_event, summary, status)
        Event-->>Fleet: 200 + updated event

        opt terminal state
            Fleet->>Event: set completed_at
        end
        Fleet-->>Agent: ACCEPTED / DUPLICATE / REJECTED
    end
